5.body:
To add a category, add the following content to the configuration file: [categories.rust]
icon = { symbol = "R", color = { rgb = 0xF74C00 } }
aliases = ["rs"]

6.body:
Custom key bindings are configured in the config file and merged with the built-in keymap. [keys.entries]
keymap = [ { on = "j", command = "entries.next", desc = "Next entry" }, { on = ["g", "g"], command = "entries.first", desc = "Go to first entry" }, { on = "up", command = "no_op" },
] See Keymap for layer names, command names, key notation, and merge behavior.

8.body:
To read the selected article with o in the Entries tab, add this to your configuration file . [keys.entries]
keymap = [ { on = "o", command = "entries.read" },
] Restart synd and select an entry. Both o and Space now open the reader. Reusing a key in the same layer replaces its default binding. To disable Space, add { on = "space", command = "no_op" } to the same array. To bind another action, put its layer name after keys. and its command name in command. You can find both under Default Key Bindings . An optional desc supplies the label when the binding appears in the status line.
